/-
  Audit/KFCausalCSpecHarmonicBornLocalNet.lean

  A FINITE LOCAL STAR-ALGEBRA NET WITH A CAUSAL BORN STATE

  This module removes the independent `localState` input from the finite
  recovered-CSpec/Hilbert interface after one honest piece of coarse-graining
  data has been fixed.  A `HarmonicSingleGenerationReadout` says which finite
  causal-growth rank is read at each recovered site and maps the actual
  finite causal children at every rank into the framework-selected 16
  single-generation outcomes.  It does not assert that this readout is the
  physically correct Standard-Model coarse graining.

  The action-selected harmonic Born law then proves nonnegativity and unit
  mass of the readout weights.  Their positive square roots canonically give
  a real-amplitude `SubstrateState singleGenDim`, hence a positive trace-one
  density matrix and exact Born compatibility.

  On a finite recovered site type, observables are site-indexed 16 by 16
  complex matrices.  The algebra of a finite region is the unital star
  subalgebra generated by observables supported in that region.  Inclusion of
  regions gives isotony.  Evaluation against the causal Born density matrix
  is a normalized positive linear functional, and its computational effects
  recover the original harmonic readout weights exactly.

  This is a finite net, not a continuum AQFT construction.  The physical
  interpretation of the readout, a compatible continuum inductive limit,
  spacelike commutativity, Wightman/OS positivity in that limit,
  spin-statistics, gauge dynamics, and the Standard-Model IR limit remain
  explicit downstream targets.

  Zero sorry. Zero custom axioms.
-/

